.TH CWE-352 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-352 \- Cross\-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)
.SH RANK
2025 CWE Top 25 rank: \fB#3\fR (2024 rank: 4).
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: Web / Session.
.SH DESCRIPTION
A state\-changing request is accepted without proof the user intended it. Because browsers attach cookies automatically, a malicious page can make a logged\-in victim's browser submit a forged request the server cannot distinguish from a legitimate one.
.SH MITIGATION
Require an unpredictable per\-session anti\-CSRF token on every state\-changing request and reject it if missing/wrong. Set session cookies SameSite=Lax or Strict, and re\-authenticate for the most sensitive actions.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB6\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2008\-4128
Cisco IOS, added 2026\-07\-13.
.PP
Cisco IOS Cross\-Site Request Forgery Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Cisco IOS 12.4 contains multiple cross\-site forgery vulnerabilities that allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary commands via (1) a certain "show privilege" command to the /level/15/exec/\- URI, and (2) a certain "alias exec" command to the /level/15/exec/\-/configure/http URI.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply vendor mitigations; follow CISA BOD 26\-04 (risk\-based patching) and forensics triage. Discontinue use if no mitigation exists.
 Due 2026\-07\-16.
.PP
